invariant: INV-14
file: tls.c
catches: unit
reason: ch_connect takes an external PSK of any length, so a device keyed
  with a short or password-length PSK falls to a dictionary attack on the
  binder of one recorded handshake (rfc9846.txt:711-720).
  test/session_hello_tests.h's row one byte under CH_PSK_LEN_MIN requires
  CH_EINVAL before a byte is sent.

--- old
    return cfg->psk != NULL && cfg->psk_len >= CH_PSK_LEN_MIN && cfg->psk_id != NULL &&
--- new
    return cfg->psk != NULL && cfg->psk_len > 0 && cfg->psk_id != NULL &&
